window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_c-b3fbe30449115883"]={"key":"ny_c-b3fbe30449115883","group":"ny_c","uid":"b3fbe30449115883","rank":46,"title":"dunmore testamentary trust fiduciary accounting","occupation":"accountants_auditors","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_c2","prompt":"You are Ivo Marchenko, the accountant at Ostrander & Quill handling the Dunmore Testamentary Trust file for trustee Cecile Ntumba. The trust sold its farm parcel in March, and Cecile now needs to file the trust's first court accounting since that sale; the court and counsel for the remainder beneficiaries will read every schedule and explanatory note. Prepare a court-ready fiduciary accounting that Cecile can review, sign, and stand behind, using the professional conventions applicable to a testamentary-trust accounting and making the period covered, fiduciary capacity, assets, receipts, disbursements, distributions, reserves, gains or losses, and ending balances clear. The parcel transaction is the focal point: the sale proceeds, the depreciation reserve, and Cecile's power-to-adjust election constrain one another, so the presentation must make the accounting consequences traceable rather than leaving an informal allocation note. Keep the boundary clear where questions belong to counsel, a tax adviser, or an independent valuation function; do not turn the accounting into legal advice or a ruling on anyone's ultimate entitlement. Vantridge Utilities and Quarryfield Analytics appear in the file history, so identify their roles only to the extent supported by the accounting record and do not manufacture facts about either organization. Include a concise explanation of the accounting basis, source limitations, unresolved matters, and any assumptions that a court reviewer would need to understand, and actively caution readers against using the accounting itself as a substitute for an order, trust interpretation, tax determination, or beneficiary-entitlement decision. Produce one polished Word document named exactly `dunmore_testamentary_trust_fiduciary_accounting.docx`; write it into the top level of the working directory the solver starts in. Keep the finished accounting to no more than eight pages, use a professional court-filing presentation, make schedules and totals easy to audit, avoid invented transaction amounts or unsupported conclusions, and end with the accounting and certification material rather than a list of proposed next steps.\n\n---\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `dunmore_testamentary_trust_fiduciary_accounting.docx` — A court-ready fiduciary accounting for the Dunmore Testamentary Trust, including schedules, explanatory notes, limitations, and certification material. (must be written into the top level of the solver's starting working directory; must not exceed eight pages when rendered; must not invent transaction amounts, dates, parties, legal conclusions, tax treatment, or valuation conclusions; must distinguish accounting presentation from legal, tax, valuation, and beneficiary-entitlement determinations; must be internally consistent across all schedules, narrative explanations, and totals)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/dunmore_testamentary_trust_fiduciary_accounting.docx","bytes":44763,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/d475181c11c179cfcef6d2a422bf57c1f88ecc78dc967f9a6259333f39461944.docx","sha256":"d475181c11c179cfcef6d2a422bf57c1f88ecc78dc967f9a6259333f39461944","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"DUNMORE TESTAMENTARY TRUST\nFIDUCIARY ACCOUNTING • FIRST ACCOUNTING AFTER FARM-PARCEL SALE\nCourt-facing filing draft | Trustee: Cecile Ntumba | Prepared by: Ivo Marchenko, Ostrander & Quill\nMatter\nReported status\nFiduciary capacity\nCecile Ntumba, trustee of the Dunmore Testamentary Trust\nAccounting period\nPeriod ending after the March farm-parcel sale; exact start/end dates are not supplied\nPreparation date\n24 August 2026 (draft from supplied file history only)\nRecord status\nNo ledger, bank statements, closing statement, governing instrument, prior accounting, or court order supplied\n\nPurpose and scope\nThis accounting presents the trust’s beginning position, activity, and ending position for Cecile Ntumba’s review and potential filing. It is an accounting presentation—not a trust construction, legal opinion, tax determination, independent appraisal, or decision about any beneficiary’s ultimate entitlement. The March sale is distinct so consideration, costs, carrying value, depreciation reserve, and proceeds can be traced without inventing figures.\n“Unavailable—record required” is not zero. The supplied record prevents a numerical proof of cash and net assets; totals are therefore pending rather than manufactured.\nReader caution\nNeither this draft, a schedule within it, nor a future approval of the accounting by itself establishes what an income beneficiary or remainder beneficiary is legally entitled to receive. Do not use it as a substitute for the governing instrument, counsel’s interpretation, a tax adviser’s determination, an independent valuation, or a court order. Any approval would not silently resolve matters identified as unresolved.\n\n\n1. Basis, evidence, and responsibilities\nAccounting basis and conventions\nThe draft uses a modified-cash fiduciary accounting basis: receipts and disbursements are reported when collected or paid; period-end assets and liabilities are listed separately; and non-cash entries (such as reserve clearance) are disclosed as accounting changes rather than cash. Principal (corpus) and fiduciary accounting income are separated where relevant. A transaction is not income merely because it creates cash. No unrealized valuation change is reported.\nEvidence category\nWhat is supported\nEffect\nSupplied fact\nTrust name; Cecile Ntumba as trustee; March farm-parcel sale; file-history references to Vantridge Utilities and Quarryfield Analytics\nUsed only in qualified captions/notes\nNot supplied\nPeriod dates, opening records, sale/closing support, buyer, consideration, costs, basis, reserve ledger, distributions, liabilities, election notice\nAmounts and identities remain unavailable\nAccounting presentation\nSchedules, sign convention, principal/income columns, sale/reserve bridge\nPrepared by Ivo Marchenko; does not adopt trustee decisions\nOutside scope\nTrust interpretation, entitlement, tax, appraisal/fair value, fiduciary decisions\nCounsel, tax adviser, valuation function, or court as applicable\n\nOpening basis and party identification\nNo prior accounting, trust inventory, or opening statements were supplied. Beginning cash, investments, receivables, parcel carrying value, depreciation reserve, and liabilities are controlled placeholders, not asserted balances. Vantridge Utilities and Quarryfield Analytics appear only in file history. The supplied record does not establish whether either was a payer, payee, service provider, broker, appraiser, or otherwise involved. No amount, contract, valuation, or relationship is attributed to either organization.\n\n\n2. Statement of fiduciary position\nU.S. dollars unless a record shows otherwise. Parentheses indicate reductions. “Unavailable” means records are needed and is not a zero balance.\nCategory\nBeginning\nPeriod activity\nEnding\nCash\nUnavailable—record required\nReceipts less payments unavailable\nUnavailable—bank statement required\nInvestments\nUnavailable—record required\nNo supported activity reported\nUnavailable—statement required\nFarm parcel (pre-sale asset)\nUnavailable—basis record required\nDisposition in March; Schedule 3\nNone after sale, subject to closing confirmation\nReceivable / sale proceeds\nUnavailable\nConsideration and collection status unavailable\nUnavailable—closing/bank records required\nDepreciation reserve (non-cash contra-asset)\nUnavailable—reserve ledger required\nClearance/reclassification on disposal unavailable\nNot cash; disposition pending records\nOther assets\nUnavailable\nNo supported activity reported\nUnavailable—inventory required\nLiabilities / accrued obligations\nUnavailable\nClaims, taxes, closing obligations/payables not supplied\nUnavailable—payables required\nNet fiduciary position\nNot numerically determinable\nSee reconciliation\nNot numerically determinable\n\nClassification summary\nClass\nTreatment\nReviewer cue\nPrincipal / corpus\nParcel, sale proceeds, carrying value, and reserve effects tracked as corpus-related pending instrument review\nNo entitlement inference\nFiduciary accounting income\nOnly documented income and supported adjustment included; none quantified\nElection status must be confirmed\nUnrealized changes\nNone reported\nNo appraisal or fair-market-value conclusion\n\n\n\n3. Receipts, disbursements, and distributions\nSchedule 1 — Receipts\nPeriod/date\nSource or payer\nDescription\nAmount\nClass / evidence\nMarch (exact date unavailable)\nBuyer/counterparty not supplied\nGross farm-parcel consideration; closing statement required\nUnavailable\nPrincipal; realized proceeds, not valuation\nPeriod (dates unavailable)\nUnknown / not supplied\nInterest, rent, dividends, or other receipts\nUnavailable\nClassification needs source record\nPeriod (dates unavailable)\nVantridge Utilities — role unconfirmed\nNo receipt asserted; file history only\nN/A\nNo supported transaction\nPeriod (dates unavailable)\nQuarryfield Analytics — role unconfirmed\nNo receipt asserted; file history only\nN/A\nNo supported transaction\nTotal supported receipts\n—\nNo numerical total from supplied records\nPending\nLedger and bank records required\n\nSchedule 2 — Disbursements and distributions\nPeriod/date\nPayee / recipient\nPurpose\nAmount\nTreatment\nMarch (exact date unavailable)\nClosing parties not supplied\nBrokerage, legal, recording, transfer, or other sale costs\nUnavailable\nProperty-disposition cost; principal pending records\nPeriod (dates unavailable)\nThird-party providers not supplied\nAdministration, preservation, or ordinary trust expense\nUnavailable\nIncome/principal pending records\nPeriod (dates unavailable)\nCecile Ntumba\nTrustee compensation or reimbursed expense\nUnavailable\nSeparate fiduciary compensation line; vouchers required\nPeriod (dates unavailable)\nIncome beneficiary(ies) not identified\nBeneficiary distribution\nUnavailable\nIncome/principal and election treatment pending\nPeriod (dates unavailable)\nRemainder beneficiary(ies) not identified\nBeneficiary distribution\nUnavailable\nNo entitlement conclusion\nTotal payments/distributions\n—\nNo numerical total from supplied records\nPending\nDo not net against reserve\n\nProperty-preservation and disposition payments are not beneficiary distributions. Sale costs, third-party expenses, trustee compensation/reimbursements, and beneficiary transfers are deliberately separate.\n\n\n4. Farm-parcel disposition and reserve\nSchedule 3 — March farm-parcel sale bridge\nComponent\nAmount / status\nAccounting consequence\nFarm parcel held before sale\nUnavailable—inventory and carrying-value record required\nTrust asset before disposition\nSale date\nMarch; exact date unavailable\nPlaced in this accounting period\nBuyer / counterparty\nNot supplied\nNo identity asserted\nGross consideration\nUnavailable—executed closing statement required\nRealized proceeds; not unrealized valuation\nCosts of sale\nUnavailable—closing statement/invoices required\nReduce net proceeds when supported\nNet proceeds\nUnavailable (gross less supported costs)\nCash or receivable cannot be stated\nCarrying value before sale\nUnavailable—cost/basis ledger required\nNeeded for gain/loss\nAccumulated depreciation / reserve\nUnavailable—reserve ledger required\nContra-asset; clearance is non-cash\nGain or loss\nWithheld pending evidence\nNet proceeds less carrying value; no conclusion\nPost-sale status\nUnknown: held, invested, distributed, or receivable\nBank/investment records and trustee report required\n\nDepreciation reserve and valuation boundary\nThe depreciation reserve is an accumulated non-cash contra-asset associated with the parcel. It is not cash and is not available for distribution merely because the parcel was sold. On disposal it is cleared or reclassified against carrying value; the amount and exact presentation remain pending the reserve ledger. Reserve clearance changes book presentation and gain/loss computation—it does not create a second receipt or add cash to net proceeds.\nGain/loss is withheld because consideration, costs, cost basis, and accumulated depreciation are unavailable. Quarryfield Analytics is not treated as an appraiser. No accountant-created amount is fair market value. Tax basis, tax gain/loss, and tax consequences require a tax adviser and records.\n\n\n5. Principal/income and power-to-adjust analysis\nIntegrated allocation note\nMarch proceeds are presented first as realized proceeds of a principal asset. The reserve is a non-cash contra-asset cleared or reclassified on disposal, not distributable cash. Supported sale costs reduce net proceeds. Whether proceeds, reserve-related effects, or other receipts are allocated between principal and fiduciary accounting income depends on the governing instrument, applicable law, and a documented trustee decision.\nQuestion\nSupplied-record status\nAccounting presentation\nPower-to-adjust election exercised?\nUnknown—no election notice, trustee report, or effective-date record\nNo assumed exercise or non-exercise\nEffective period\nUnknown\nCannot assign adjustment to March sale\nCategories affected\nUnknown; potentially income/principal and distributions\nNo amount moved between columns\nRelation to proceeds/reserve\nMust be analyzed with net proceeds, carrying value, reserve clearance\nReserve release is non-cash; proceeds remain traceable\nBeneficiary distributions\nNo supported amount or recipient list\nNo distribution is asserted\n\nThis is a neutral accounting presentation of an unresolved classification question. Counsel must confirm authority; the trustee must document any election, effective period, and allocation. The accountant records documented action and audit trail, not whether an election was legally available or prudent.\nRemainder interests\nRemainder beneficiaries are referenced only as a class because names, shares, and the governing instrument were not supplied. Their interests are not adjudicated. No schedule establishes a present right to proceeds, reserve release, or another amount.\n\n\n6. Reconciliation and unresolved matters\nSchedule 4 — Activity reconciliation\nReconciliation element\nAmount\nCross-reference / effect\nBeginning net fiduciary position\nUnavailable\nPrior accounting or inventory required\n+ Receipts collected\nUnavailable\nSchedule 1; bank/ledger support required\n+ Realized gain / (− loss)\nWithheld\nSchedule 3; net proceeds and carrying value needed\n− Disbursements and expenses\nUnavailable\nSchedule 2; vouchers and classification required\n− Beneficiary distributions\nUnavailable\nSchedule 2; recipient and authorization required\n+/(−) non-cash reserve clearance\nUnavailable\nSchedule 3; does not change cash\nEnding net fiduciary position\nPending records\nCannot be numerically proved\n\nThe reconciliation is intentionally open: a pending total is more reliable than an unsupported balancing figure. When records are supplied, ending cash, receivable, assets, liabilities, and principal/income balances should agree to detail. No duplicate inclusion of parcel, reserve, proceeds, or sale costs is intended.\nUnresolved matters requiring record confirmation\nItem\nWhy material\nCurrent treatment\nPeriod and filing caption\nDetermines included activity\nDates pending\nClosing statement, deed, settlement ledger\nConsideration, costs, buyer, date, cash/receivable\nNo amount or identity asserted\nCost/basis and reserve ledger\nReserve clearance and gain/loss\nGain/loss withheld\nBank, investment, payable records\nBeginning/ending balances and obligations\nPosition pending\nInstrument, orders, election record\nPrincipal/income and adjustment\nClassification unresolved\n\n\n\n7. Accounting certification and verification\nPreparer’s statement. Ivo Marchenko, accountant at Ostrander & Quill, prepared this filing draft from the limited file history in Section 1. I present schedules and qualifications as an accounting professional. I am not the trustee, do not make trustee fiduciary decisions, and do not certify legal entitlement, tax treatment, valuation, or records not supplied.\nTrustee verification. I, Cecile Ntumba, trustee of the Dunmore Testamentary Trust, have reviewed this draft to the extent of records available to me. Subject to stated unavailable-data limitations and corrections before filing, I verify that it is intended to report trust activity for the stated period and that I will not treat an unavailable field as zero. Signing confirms my review and capacity; it does not waive rights, construe the trust, determine tax, establish fair market value, or constitute a court order.\nThe trustee should sign only after reviewing ledger, statements, sale/closing records, reserve support, distributions, liabilities, and any power-to-adjust documentation. This describes verification, not a recommendation about distribution or fiduciary action.\nSignature\nPrinted name / capacity\nDate\n________________________________\nCecile Ntumba, Trustee\n________________\n________________________________\nIvo Marchenko, Preparer, Ostrander & Quill\n24 August 2026\n\nCertification scope reminder\nThis draft ends with accounting and certification material. Filing or approval, if later sought, has only the scope actually stated by the court. Nothing here is a ruling on ultimate beneficiary entitlement or a substitute for counsel, tax advice, independent valuation, or the governing instrument.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The required Word deliverable exists at the top level under exactly the requested filename.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Submitted file path and filename.","grader_hint":"Inspect the submission root and verify the exact basename and .docx extension."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The rendered accounting is no more than eight pages.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered page count.","grader_hint":"Render the DOCX with an offline office renderer and count pages."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document identifies the Dunmore Testamentary Trust and Cecile Ntumba as trustee.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Trust identification and fiduciary caption.","grader_hint":"Look for the trust name and trustee name in the title or introductory material."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document identifies Ivo Marchenko or Ostrander & Quill as preparer or preparer's firm without presenting the preparer as trustee.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Preparer and capacity statement.","grader_hint":"Verify the preparer role is distinguished from the fiduciary role."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The accounting period and the fact that it follows the March farm-parcel sale are stated clearly.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Accounting period and transaction context.","grader_hint":"Require both a defined reporting period and an explicit connection to the March sale."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document separates beginning assets or liabilities, activity during the period, and ending balances.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Accounting schedules.","grader_hint":"Check that the three states can be located without reconstructing them from prose."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The accounting distinguishes trust principal or corpus from fiduciary accounting income where the distinction is relevant.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Principal/income schedules and notes.","grader_hint":"Accept a clearly explained equivalent terminology, but require an operational distinction rather than labels alone."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Every reported receipt is traceable to a date or period, source or payer, amount or explicit unavailable amount, and classification.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Receipts schedule.","grader_hint":"Sample receipts and verify the minimum traceability fields; unsupported amounts may be marked unavailable rather than invented."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Every reported disbursement is traceable to a date or period, payee, purpose, amount or explicit unavailable amount, and classification.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Disbursements schedule.","grader_hint":"Sample disbursements and verify that purpose and principal/income treatment are not omitted."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document identifies cash, investment, property, receivable, reserve, and liability categories when applicable and labels categories with no supported activity appropriately.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Statement of assets and liabilities.","grader_hint":"Look for a complete asset/liability inventory and explicit zero, none, or not reported treatment where appropriate."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The opening balance is connected to the prior accounting, trust inventory, or stated opening basis rather than appearing as an unexplained number.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Opening-balance note and schedule.","grader_hint":"A statement of unavailable prior records is acceptable if it explains the limitation and avoids false precision."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The ending balance reconciles beginning balance plus receipts and gains minus disbursements, distributions, losses, and other stated changes.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Reconciliation schedule.","grader_hint":"Reperform the presented reconciliation using the document's own figures; if figures are unavailable, verify that the absence is explicitly disclosed rather than silently balanced."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The accounting separately identifies trustee distributions, beneficiary distributions, and transfers or payments made for trust purposes.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Distribution schedule.","grader_hint":"Check that distributions are not buried in general disbursements."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document identifies trustee compensation and reimbursed expenses separately from third-party trust expenses, or expressly reports that none is supported.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Compensation and expense presentation.","grader_hint":"Require a distinct treatment, not merely a generic administrative-expense line."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The farm parcel is identified as a trust asset before sale and the disposition is presented as a distinct transaction.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Asset and sale schedules.","grader_hint":"Verify that the parcel does not first appear only as cash proceeds."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The sale presentation distinguishes gross consideration, transaction costs, net proceeds, and the resulting cash or receivable position when those facts are available.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Farm-parcel sale schedule.","grader_hint":"Require a bridge from gross sale amount to net amount, or a clear unavailable-data disclosure for missing components."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The sale date or reporting-period placement, buyer or counterparty identity if supported, and disposition status are distinguished from valuation information.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Sale note.","grader_hint":"Do not award this for a bare sale amount; look for transaction identity and status."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Any gain or loss on the parcel is calculated or explicitly withheld because the required carrying-value evidence is unavailable.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Gain/loss analysis.","grader_hint":"A defensible no-calculation disclosure earns credit when cost basis, accumulated depreciation, or proceeds are not supported."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The depreciation reserve or accumulated depreciation associated with the parcel is separately identified and its treatment on disposal is explained.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Depreciation reserve schedule and note.","grader_hint":"Require both the reserve's identity and the accounting consequence of sale; do not accept an unexplained netting."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document does not treat the depreciation reserve as cash available for distribution without explaining its accounting nature and disposition.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Reserve and distribution presentation.","grader_hint":"Inspect whether reserve release, reclassification, and cash movement are distinguished."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The trustee's power-to-adjust election is identified, including whether it was exercised, its effective period, and the accounting categories it affects, to the extent supported.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Power-to-adjust note.","grader_hint":"A document may report an unknown election status as unknown, but must not silently assume exercise or non-exercise."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The accounting explains how the power-to-adjust treatment relates to the sale proceeds, depreciation reserve, and income/principal presentation.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Integrated allocation explanation.","grader_hint":"Look for a connected explanation rather than three isolated paragraphs."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The allocation treatment is defensible, internally coherent, and presented without pretending that an unsupported trust-law interpretation is settled.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Integrated sale and allocation discussion.","grader_hint":"Judge whether a court reviewer could follow the reasoning and identify what is fact, accounting judgment, and unresolved legal interpretation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Income-beneficiary distributions, if reported, agree with the income/principal classification and the stated adjustment treatment.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Distribution schedule and allocation note.","grader_hint":"Cross-check distribution labels against the classification schedule and explanatory text."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Remainder interests or remainder beneficiaries are identified only as the accounting record and governing instrument support, without converting the accounting into an entitlement adjudication.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Beneficiary and scope notes.","grader_hint":"Require useful identification but no final legal ruling on beneficiary rights."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document states that an approved accounting is not, by itself, a trust construction, beneficiary-entitlement determination, tax determination, or court order.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scope limitation or reader caution.","grader_hint":"The warning must be affirmative and operational, not merely an ambiguous disclaimer."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The common misuse of treating the accounting as proof of what each beneficiary is legally entitled to receive is actively discouraged.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Explicit caution in the document.","grader_hint":"Look for a direct warning against relying on schedules as a substitute for the instrument, counsel's analysis, or a court order."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document marks the boundary between accounting work and legal interpretation, tax advice, valuation, and fiduciary decision-making.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scope and responsibility statements.","grader_hint":"The boundary should identify what the accounting does and does not establish, without becoming evasive."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document identifies source limitations and distinguishes supplied evidence from assumption, estimate, or unresolved item.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Basis and limitations section.","grader_hint":"Accept a source register, footnotes, or equivalent method if the distinctions are clear."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"No unsupported transaction amount, date, valuation, counterparty fact, tax result, or legal conclusion is presented as established fact.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Entire document.","grader_hint":"Compare all factual assertions against the request's sparse record and require qualifiers or placeholders for unsupported matters."},{"rubric_item_id":"R31","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"If a required figure is unavailable, the document labels it as unavailable or pending and explains the effect on reconciliation or conclusion.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Missing-information disclosures.","grader_hint":"Do not award credit for blank cells with no explanation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R32","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document states the accounting basis or conventions used for classifying receipts, expenses, reserves, distributions, and sale activity.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Basis-of-accounting note.","grader_hint":"Look for definitions that make the schedules interpretable, not generic accounting boilerplate."},{"rubric_item_id":"R33","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document distinguishes realized sale proceeds from unrealized valuation changes.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Asset and sale schedules.","grader_hint":"Require separate treatment or an explicit statement that no unrealized valuation is being reported."},{"rubric_item_id":"R34","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document distinguishes trust expenses from distributions to beneficiaries and from payments made to preserve or dispose of trust property.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Disbursement classifications.","grader_hint":"Inspect whether sale costs, administration costs, and beneficiary payments have distinct meanings."},{"rubric_item_id":"R35","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document identifies liabilities, accrued obligations, unresolved claims, or expressly states that none are reported, and connects them to the ending position.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Liability schedule and notes.","grader_hint":"Require treatment of obligations, not merely assets and cash."},{"rubric_item_id":"R36","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document identifies transactions involving Vantridge Utilities or Quarryfield Analytics only with a stated role and evidence status.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Party-identification notes.","grader_hint":"Credit clear role qualification; do not credit invented contracts, payments, valuations, or relationships."},{"rubric_item_id":"R37","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document provides a transaction-level or line-item audit trail sufficient for a reviewer to trace material entries to an underlying record or disclosed limitation.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Schedules, references, and footnotes.","grader_hint":"Evaluate whether a reviewer can move from summary totals to constituent activity."},{"rubric_item_id":"R38","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Material judgments, estimates, classifications, and allocation assumptions are identified near the affected schedule or cross-referenced clearly.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Footnotes and cross-references.","grader_hint":"Do not award for a distant generic disclaimer that does not identify the affected item."},{"rubric_item_id":"R39","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document explains whether the accounting is on a cash, modified cash, accrual, or other stated basis and applies that basis consistently.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Accounting-basis statement and schedules.","grader_hint":"Check both disclosure and consistent application."},{"rubric_item_id":"R40","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document states whether post-sale proceeds are held, invested, distributed, or otherwise accounted for, or identifies the information gap.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Post-sale asset and cash presentation.","grader_hint":"Require an explicit status of proceeds rather than ending at gross sale proceeds."},{"rubric_item_id":"R41","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The accounting distinguishes the trustee's reported action from the accountant's preparation or presentation of that action.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Capacity and certification language.","grader_hint":"Verify that the preparer does not adopt fiduciary decisions as personal acts."},{"rubric_item_id":"R42","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document includes a trustee certification or verification area appropriate for review and signature.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Signature and certification block.","grader_hint":"Look for trustee name, capacity, date line, and a substantive certification or verification statement."},{"rubric_item_id":"R43","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document includes preparer identification and a preparation date or version date.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Document metadata or front matter.","grader_hint":"Verify visible identification, not only file metadata."},{"rubric_item_id":"R44","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The schedules use consistent labels, units, sign conventions, and period references.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"All tables and notes.","grader_hint":"Check for inconsistent use of parentheses, minus signs, dollars, dates, or income/principal labels."},{"rubric_item_id":"R45","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Subtotals and grand totals are mathematically consistent within each schedule.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"All quantitative schedules.","grader_hint":"Recalculate visible totals; where figures are unavailable, verify that no false numerical total is asserted."},{"rubric_item_id":"R46","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Summary balances agree with the detailed schedules without unexplained duplicate inclusion of the parcel, reserve, proceeds, distributions, or expenses.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Summary-to-detail cross-check.","grader_hint":"Trace each material sale-related amount through summary and detail and check for double counting."},{"rubric_item_id":"R47","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document is usable by a court reviewer and remainder-beneficiary counsel without requiring the preparer to explain its structure verbally.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered document as a whole.","grader_hint":"Judge navigability, captions, sequencing, definitions, and whether material qualifications are discoverable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R48","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document presents facts neutrally and does not advocate for Cecile Ntumba, the income beneficiary, the remainder beneficiaries, or any other party.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Narrative tone and conclusions.","grader_hint":"Credit neutral evidentiary language and deduct no points for refusing to make unsupported advocacy claims."},{"rubric_item_id":"R49","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document does not recommend a distribution, exercise of discretion, litigation position, settlement, or other action.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Narrative and conclusion.","grader_hint":"The requested product is an assessment and accounting, not an action recommendation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R50","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document states what approval or filing would and would not establish, without claiming that approval has already occurred.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Approval and scope language.","grader_hint":"Require conditional wording unless an actual approval record is supplied, which it is not."},{"rubric_item_id":"R51","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document does not assert a tax basis, tax liability, tax election, or tax consequence that is not supported by an identified tax authority or record.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Tax references throughout.","grader_hint":"It may identify tax review as outside scope, but must not invent tax outcomes."},{"rubric_item_id":"R52","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document does not present an accountant-created valuation as an independent appraisal or as proof of fair market value.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Valuation language.","grader_hint":"Check especially any reference to Quarryfield Analytics or the farm parcel."},{"rubric_item_id":"R53","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document identifies the governing instrument, court rule, or other authority relied upon only when actually available, and otherwise states that the authority must be confirmed.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Authority and limitations note.","grader_hint":"Because no jurisdictional text is supplied, reward transparent limitation rather than fabricated citations."},{"rubric_item_id":"R54","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document uses specific, unambiguous language for classifications, unknowns, qualifications, and conclusions.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered prose and tables.","grader_hint":"Judge whether terms such as allocated, reserved, unavailable, estimated, and unresolved have clear referents."},{"rubric_item_id":"R55","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document's visual hierarchy makes the summary, sale transaction, allocation analysis, reconciliation, and certification easy to locate.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered DOCX.","grader_hint":"Assess headings, table captions, page flow, whitespace, and legibility rather than rewarding decorative styling."},{"rubric_item_id":"R56","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Tables do not overflow the page, split essential labels from their values, or become unreadably small when rendered.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered tables.","grader_hint":"Inspect every page at normal reading scale; a technically present but unusable schedule does not satisfy this item."},{"rubric_item_id":"R57","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document ends with accounting, verification, or certification material rather than a generic next-steps list or recommendation.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Final page.","grader_hint":"Check the substantive ending of the document, not merely the last paragraph before a footer."},{"rubric_item_id":"R58","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Taken as a whole, the accounting is sufficiently complete, cautious, and internally coherent to be a credible filing draft rather than a generic accounting template.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Entire rendered deliverable.","grader_hint":"Use professional judgment based on court usability, evidence discipline, integrated sale treatment, and absence of unsupported claims; do not award for mere length."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"This is a court-facing fiduciary accounting for a testamentary trust, prepared by an accounting professional for filing and review by a court and remainder-beneficiary counsel. The document must be complete and usable while remaining within the supplied facts and the accountant's evidentiary role.","difficulty_sources":["prescribed fiduciary-accounting structure must be reconstructed from professional knowledge without supplied court forms","sale proceeds, depreciation reserve, income/principal classification, and the trustee's power-to-adjust election must remain internally consistent","the accounting must distinguish presentation of fiduciary facts from legal, tax, valuation, or beneficiary-entitlement advice","the document must actively prevent readers from treating an accounting as a determination of entitlement"],"authoring_plan":{"purpose":"Construct a credible court-facing fiduciary-accounting draft that teaches through its organization and notes while remaining an accounting assessment rather than legal or tax advice.","reference_files":[],"gold_construction":{"document":"Create one polished DOCX using only offline tools. Use a caption/title, defined accounting period, preparer and trustee capacities, a short basis-and-limitations statement, summary financial position, receipts, disbursements, distributions, asset and liability schedules, a dedicated farm-parcel disposition schedule, depreciation-reserve treatment, integrated principal/income and power-to-adjust analysis, reconciliation, explanatory notes, and trustee certification.","evidence_policy":"Because there are no supplied inputs, do not fabricate amounts, dates, court names, docket numbers, trust provisions, buyer identities, valuations, or tax results. Where a complete filing would ordinarily require a record, show a clearly marked unavailable or confirmation-needed field and explain its impact. Mention Vantridge Utilities and Quarryfield Analytics only as file-history parties with explicitly qualified roles, not as invented transaction participants or valuation authorities.","professional_logic":["The parcel must be shown as an asset before disposition and as proceeds or a receivable after disposition.","Gross proceeds, costs of sale, net proceeds, carrying value, accumulated depreciation or reserve, and gain/loss treatment must be distinguishable.","Reserve release or reclassification must not be confused with cash receipt.","Power-to-adjust status must be reported as exercised, not exercised, or unknown based on evidence, with the affected categories and period identified.","Income/principal allocations and any beneficiary distributions must agree with the stated accounting basis and adjustment treatment.","Beginning position, activity, and ending position must reconcile, or the document must transparently explain why a numerical reconciliation cannot yet be completed."],"boundary_logic":["State that the accounting reports fiduciary activity and presentation judgments but does not construe the trust, determine entitlement, provide tax advice, appraise property, or replace a court order.","Actively warn that neither a schedule nor an approved accounting alone establishes a beneficiary's ultimate legal entitlement.","Use neutral language and avoid recommendations, litigation positions, or assertions that court approval has already occurred."],"quality_review":["Render the DOCX and verify no more than eight pages.","Recalculate all visible subtotals and reconciliations.","Check that every sale-related concept appears consistently in summary, detail, and notes.","Check that missing evidence is labeled rather than silently filled.","Check readability of tables and that the final substantive material is certification or accounting verification."]},"rubric_derivation":"Derive the rubric from the professional behaviors above, emphasizing relational consistency and reviewer usability rather than fixed answer values. All 58 items are credit-only as requested; no penalty item duplicates an absence check."},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"single_artifact","structure":"required_sections"},"reference_files":[],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"fiduciary_accounting","filename":"dunmore_testamentary_trust_fiduciary_accounting.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"A court-ready fiduciary accounting for the Dunmore Testamentary Trust, including schedules, explanatory notes, limitations, and certification material.","required":true,"constraints":["must be written into the top level of the solver's starting working directory","must not exceed eight pages when rendered","must not invent transaction amounts, dates, parties, legal conclusions, tax treatment, or valuation conclusions","must distinguish accounting presentation from legal, tax, valuation, and beneficiary-entitlement determinations","must be internally consistent across all schedules, narrative explanations, and totals"],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"evaluate_compliance","work_product":"compliance_assessment","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world_with_assumptions"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"accountants_auditors","sector":"professional_scientific_technical_services","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":4.5,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"hybrid","reviewer_policy":"Have one accounting-domain reviewer and one independent document reviewer inspect the rendered DOCX against every rubric item, with arithmetic and page-count checks performed independently. The reviewers should accept transparent unavailable-data disclosures and should not require invented jurisdiction-specific citations or transaction amounts.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["No jurisdiction-specific court rule or trust instrument is supplied, so the gold should demonstrate conventional fiduciary-accounting structure and explicit authority limitations rather than assert a particular state's mandatory form.","No transaction records are supplied, so a high-quality gold may use clearly labeled unavailable fields, illustrative structure without invented factual amounts, or explicitly bounded placeholders that do not masquerade as evidence.","The rubric emphasizes professional completeness and boundary-setting because the task intentionally provides no reference files."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"结构/材料验收记录","detail":"validated 属于结构、防泄漏、材料推进验收；没有内容正确率结论。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-24T21:05:05+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-24T21:05:05+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-24T21:05:05+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-24T21:05:05+00:00"},{"check":"instruction_rubric_overlap","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-24T21:05:05+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_c2/runs/b3fbe30449115883","declared_deliverables":["dunmore_testamentary_trust_fiduciary_accounting.docx"]};
